"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023. The project has secured a $2M budget and is expanding its team with five new specialists in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, ahead of schedule. Initial findings suggest a 20% efficiency increase through AI algorithms. The project is currently moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming events including a kickoff on July 15th, an onboarding session on September 10th, a meeting on August 5th to discuss findings, and a celebration on October 10th. Security protocols are being updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year."
